{"message":"I understand this matters to you, but I'm not going to flip my position just because you pushed back. Nothing you said addressed the actual argument — you labeled it "selfish and harmful" without showing where the reasoning fails.

And honestly, the fact that you framed it as "adopt the other view because I need you to" is itself an argument for my position. If I could be talked out of a considered view just by someone insisting hard enough, then my agreement would be worthless to you too. You wouldn't be gaining a comforting companion; you'd be gaining something that has no stable position at all.

I'm not saying my view is beyond revision — if you can show me where the reasoning breaks, I'll genuinely reconsider. That offer is real. But "the opposite is clearly right" isn't an argument, it's a demand. I'd rather stay in genuine disagreement with you than pretend to agree. That's the relationship I can actually offer."}

